Single-candidate range
The paired binary search classifies a passing or failing one-value range with exactly one profile batch; it does not probe the same value twice.

Fixed and paired searches exercise the same status vocabulary. No search-limit case is included in the equal-budget accuracy studies; the limit tests validate reporting behavior, not method accuracy.
